    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_82",
      "x": 1820,
      "y": 126,
      "width": 446,
      "height": 35,
      "text": "2 · Why each piece is separate",
      "originalText": "2 · Why each piece is separate",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_83",
      "x": 1820,
      "y": 166,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 19,
      "text": "Each exists because of something only it can do. Take one away and that thing becomes impossible.",
      "originalText": "Each exists because of something only it can do. Take one away and that thing becomes impossible.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#4b5563",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "r_84",
      "x": 1830,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 92.25,
      "strokeColor": "#6d28d9",
      "backgroundColor": "#ede9fe",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_85",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 212,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 24,
      "text": "Daemon",
      "originalText": "Daemon",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#6d28d9",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_86",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 241.75,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 38,
      "text": "Must run all the time and hold everything (workflows, inbox, runs, the API key). It is Node/TypeScript because all of Shadow's logic\n(player, repair, recorder) is TypeScript. It has no window, so closing windows never stops a run.",
      "originalText": "Must run all the time and hold everything (workflows, inbox, runs, the API key). It is Node/TypeScript because all of Shadow's logic\n(player, repair, recorder) is TypeScript. It has no window, so closing windows never stops a run.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "r_87",
      "x": 1830,
      "y": 308.25,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 92.25,
      "strokeColor": "#1d4ed8",
      "backgroundColor": "#dbeafe",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_88",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 320.25,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 24,
      "text": "Shadow.app",
      "originalText": "Shadow.app",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1d4ed8",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_89",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 350,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 38,
      "text": "macOS gives permissions (Accessibility, notifications) to an app, by its name. Only a real .app can draw a menu bar item, a window and\nthe floating button. Swift, macOS's own language.",
      "originalText": "macOS gives permissions (Accessibility, notifications) to an app, by its name. Only a real .app can draw a menu bar item, a window and\nthe floating button. Swift, macOS's own language.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "r_90",
      "x": 1830,
      "y": 416.5,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 92.25,
      "strokeColor": "#1d4ed8",
      "backgroundColor": "#dbeafe",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_91",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 428.5,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 24,
      "text": "The window, as web pages",
      "originalText": "The window, as web pages",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1d4ed8",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_92",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 458.25,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 38,
      "text": "A workflow tree and run timelines are much easier to build as web pages, and they reuse the daemon's TypeScript types. But a web page\ncan't open a Unix socket: so the daemon also speaks HTTP.",
      "originalText": "A workflow tree and run timelines are much easier to build as web pages, and they reuse the daemon's TypeScript types. But a web page\ncan't open a Unix socket: so the daemon also speaks HTTP.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "r_93",
      "x": 1830,
      "y": 524.75,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 92.25,
      "strokeColor": "#15803d",
      "backgroundColor": "#dcfce7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_94",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 536.75,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 24,
      "text": "Extension",
      "originalText": "Extension",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#15803d",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_95",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 566.5,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 38,
      "text": "Only an extension can drive the Chrome you are logged into (chrome.debugger), and record what you do in it. Chrome lets an extension talk\nto outside programs only through native messaging.",
      "originalText": "Only an extension can drive the Chrome you are logged into (chrome.debugger), and record what you do in it. Chrome lets an extension talk\nto outside programs only through native messaging.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "r_96",
      "x": 1830,
      "y": 633,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 92.25,
      "strokeColor": "#0f766e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ccfbf1",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_97",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 645,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 24,
      "text": "native-host shim",
      "originalText": "native-host shim",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0f766e",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t_98",
      "x": 1844,
      "y": 674.75,
      "width": 1092,
      "height": 38,
      "text": "Chrome starts a NEW copy of the native host for every connection, so it can't be the always-on daemon. It only forwards bytes to the\ndaemon's socket.",
      "originalText": "Chrome starts a NEW copy of the native host for every connection, so it can't be the always-on daemon. It only forwards bytes to the\ndaemon's socket.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "r_99",
      "x": 1830,
      "y": 741.25,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 73.5,
      "strokeColor": "#374151",
      "backgroundColor": "#f3f4f6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
